{{Administrative levels and divisions of Burawa sidebar}}


[[Burawa]] is divided into three levels of administrative divisions that have been formed after the 1967 [[Administration Reorganization Act (Burawa)|Administration Reorganization Act]]. The act created a three level administrative system composed of administrations and communes with a special community level system for some areas.

There are 86 independent urban administrations, 34 rural administrations, and 8 metropolitan administrations in Burawa that lie on the top level, each administration is equal to a seat in the [[Senate of Burawa]]. Urban administrations are split into two types, dependent and independent urban administrations, dependent urban administrations are part of metropolitan administrations but have the same level of autonomy as independent urban administrations that are not part of metropolitan administrations. Metropolitan administrations have a level of equal autonomy to their dependent urban administrations but operate as a supporting entity to decisions made by the urban administration.


== Administrations ==
Administrations are the top level of government in Burawa. Administrations are categorized into three categories, urban administrations, metropolitan administrations and rural administrations. Each administration type has different rules that determine funding, management and policy decision making in each region. Administration leadership are elected by the representatives of legislative districts within the an administrative area.

