=== Urban Administrations ===
There are 86 independent urban administrations and 102 dependent urban administrations that are part of Metropolitan administrations. Urban Administrations function as city-level administrators of locals within Burawa, they are in charge of all services, utilities and management of civil services within their locale.

An urban administration is formed when a group of neighboring communes reach a population of over 100,000 people or a density of over 400 people per square km, below that the communes are either part of another urban administration or are part of a rural administration. The largest urban administration by population and area is [[Khar]] with an area of 225 sq mi (582.7 km2), and population of 1.7 million people, the smallest urban administration is [[Filal]], with a population of 68,404, and was established after the 2025 census in the [[Whar]] rural administration.

=== Rural Administrations ===
Rural administrations are independent bodies that manage areas considered rural; communes and clusters of communes that have a contiguous group of populations that less than 100,000 people and a density of lower than 400 people per square km. 13% of Burawa's population lives within a rural administration. Rural administrations can establish special sub-districts known as [[Townships in Burawa|townships]] that are groups of communes that can form a city-like administration.

There are 34 rural administrations, divided up generally by geographic features, then split by population center grouping. Rural administrations have greater power than urban and metropolitan administrations as they manage a larger area of land, most rural administrations will have informal sub-districts to assist in better management of regions alongside townships.

==== Townships ====
Townships are special sub-administrative divisions of Rural Administrations, they exist to manage population centers that were formerly towns, villages and small cities that exist in the administration. Townships generally have the same administrative rights as an urban administration, but do not have the say in regional policies.

=== Communes ===
{{Main|Communes in Burawa}}
Communes administrative divisions in Burawa that are treated as districts of a administration, they can vary in population and size. Communes are the building blocks of legislative districts, which send members to the lower house of Burawa, legislative districts can be at most the population of Burawa divided by 796 seats in the [[Lower House of Burawa]] (158,253 persons as of 2025). Communes must wholey fit within a legislative boundary, thus must always be smaller or the same size as a legislative boundary, the median commune has a population of 62,000, and there an average of 3.7 communes per legislative district.

Commune administrators are elected by direct election from citizens of a commune, a commune has a council of 7 members.

=== Communities ===
{{Main|Communities in Burawa}}
Communities is a subdivision of a commune that exist in larger communes that assist in hyperlocal administration of a locale. There are currently 10,439 communities in Burawa. Communities are headed by a community council of 3 members that are voted directly by the citizens of a locale.